  {
   "id": "22b4c0f6-4328-4636-ae99-0084e0794fe3",
   "type": "playlists",
   "attributes": {
    "name": "The World of: Radiohead’s ‘OK Computer’",
    "description": "“Fitter, happier, more productive” … Was any work of pop-music art more prescient in the late ’90s, or in any epoch, than Radiohead’s third studio LP? Released in 1997, its ironic dichotomy — a fearful meditation on tech-dependent postmodern life, awash in ingenious futuristic sounds and recording strategies — seems to embody our contemporary world of forced wellness and smartphone addiction. To celebrate the 25th anniversary of this essential album, we researched this special ‘World of’ playlist featuring the original tracks, their specific sonic and musical inspirations, the band’s more general influences during the period, other songs from this important moment in British alternative rock and more. \n",
    "bounded": true,
    "duration": "PT2H46M30S",
