  {
   "id": "2bf56688-c693-47a2-839f-aa18bd333c24",
   "type": "playlists",
   "attributes": {
    "name": "Radiohead Essentials",
    "description": "Modern rock history wouldn’t have been the same without Radiohead – a British ‘90s sensation that became one of the most influential alternative bands of all time. The five members – Thom Yorke (vocals, guitar), Ed O'Brien (guitar, vocals), Jonny Greenwood (guitar), Colin Greenwood (bass), and Phil Selway (drums) – formed Radiohead in 1988 while attending boarding school in Oxford. Initially called ‘On a Friday’ (referring to the day of the week they would meet up to rehearse) the band began a musical career that sharply took off with the celebrated 1993 debut Pablo Honey (and hit single “Creep”) and the classic follow-up The Bends (1995). But it was with the progressive, timeless, electronic-tinged masterpiece OK Computer (1997) that Radiohead became an international phenomenon. Since then, the band has brilliantly managed to continually evolve and reinvent themselves, always trying out new sounds and musical directions, such as with the two-part electronic suite Kid A (2000) and Amnesiac (2001). As one of the most celebrated acts of their time, Radiohead have never really made a mediocre album. (Photo: Rovi)",
