  {
   "id": "549e6e94-05f2-4c5c-91d5-92a08a03665a",
   "type": "playlists",
   "attributes": {
    "name": "Remember...the 1990s",
    "description": "The 1990s - what a memorable decade! R.E.M. and U2 ascended as world stars, while grunge changed many people's perception of what could top the charts. Pop-punk (Green Day, The Offspring) and Britpop (Oasis, Blur) were born, just as hip-hop was gaining traction on the charts (Jay-Z, Eminem). Many promising hitmakers would go on to have long, healthy careers, while others would never see the 2000s. But they all belong in our collective memory of the 1990's. (Cover: The Notorious B.I.G. - Ready to Die, Bad Boy/WMG)",
